            <ArticleTitle>Emotional pain without sensory pain--dream on?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>153-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.neuron.2009.01.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The article by Danziger and colleagues in this issue of Neuron evaluates empathy in a unique population--individuals with congenital insensitivity to pain. As such, it provides insights into the brain's ability to evaluate others' feeling to observed pain without having a specific sensory experience of pain itself.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
